# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 59-62 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 10 — CHAPTER 12, 2026-09-20; the one run): the header (59), the destruction (60-61), the
# place sought (62) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation of the shelf CUT by consonants (ch12_ink.SP_ — a miss lands in
# FAIL, asserted empty by the ledger writer); a middah named only where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, the code checked before it is typed); the rows
# read before at earlier sittings marked REREAD WHOLE. Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT rows terse. Chapter 11's form (ch11_rows_sifrei_37_38.py).
from ch12_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(59, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THESE ARE THE STATUTES" (12:1) — THESE ARE THE MIDRASHOT (THE EXPOSITIONS). The head row of piska 59, THE FIRST ON THE CHAPTER ({SP_(59, 1, "אלו", "המדרשות")} "these are the expositions"): the header\'s first noun read as the rules derived by exposition — THE INK: "these are the statutes and the judgments" stands at 12:1 and Leviticus 26:46 alone (computed), the fold\'s footer the header\'s twin; 58:1 read the same nouns at 11:32. Fresh.')
srow(59, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE JUDGMENTS" — THESE ARE THE LAWS (THE DINIM). ({SP_(59, 2, "אלו", "הדינים")} "these are the laws"). Fresh.')
srow(59, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH YOU SHALL KEEP" — THIS IS MISHNAH (THE ORAL LEARNING). ({SP_(59, 3, "זו", "משנה")} "this is mishnah"). Fresh.')
srow(59, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO DO" — THIS IS THE DEED. ({SP_(59, 4, "זו", "מעשה")} "this is the deed"): the four nouns of the header the four layers — exposition, law, learning, deed. Fresh.')
srow(59, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE LAND" — MIGHT ALL THE COMMANDMENTS APPLY OUTSIDE THE LAND? "TO DO IN THE LAND." MIGHT NONE APPLY BUT IN THE LAND? "ALL THE DAYS THAT YOU LIVE ON THE EARTH." AFTER INCLUDING, THE VERSE LIMITED — WE LEARN FROM WHAT IS SAID IN THE CONTEXT: "DESTROY, YOU SHALL DESTROY ALL THE PLACES" (12:2) — AS IDOLATRY IS A DUTY OF THE BODY NOT BOUND TO THE LAND AND APPLIES IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE IT, SO EVERY DUTY OF THE BODY; THE LAND-BOUND APPLY ONLY IN THE LAND, EXCEPT ORLAH AND MIXED SEEDS; R. ELIEZER ADDS THE NEW GRAIN. THE RULE OF THE LAND-BOUND COMMANDMENTS from the header\'s two clauses ({SP_(59, 5, "מצות", "הגוף", "ואינה", "תלויה", "בארץ")} "a duty of the body not bound to the land"; {SP_(59, 5, "חוץ", "מן", "הערלה", "והכלאים")} "except orlah and mixed seeds"): I12 (checked — the matter learned from its context), the destruction of the shrines the paradigm; Mishnah Kiddushin 1:9 the answer sheet (the English notes it; Kiddushin 36b-37a at 10b\'s docket) — read at 44:1 on 11:18 at chapter 11 in the same words. Fresh.')

srow(60, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"DESTROY, YOU SHALL DESTROY" (12:2) — IF ONE CUT DOWN AN ASHERAH AND IT GREW BACK EVEN TEN TIMES, HE MUST CUT IT DOWN AGAIN. The doubled verb read as repetition ({SP_(60, 1, "אפלו", "עשר", "פעמים")} "even ten times"): THE INK — the infinitive absolute + imperfect, the chapter\'s one (computed); the same doubling is "perish, you shall perish" at 4:26, 8:19, 30:18 (computed) — Israel\'s perishing turned on the shrines. Fresh.')
srow(60, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"ALL THE PLACES WHERE THEY SERVED" — IT TELLS THAT THE CANAANITES WERE STEEPED IN IDOLATRY MORE THAN ALL THE NATIONS. ({SP_(60, 2, "שטופים", "בעבודה", "זרה")} "steeped in idolatry"). Fresh.')
srow(60, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH YOU ARE DISPOSSESSING — THEIR GODS": WHY DO YOU DISPOSSESS? BECAUSE OF THEIR GODS — THAT YOU NOT DO AS THEY DID AND OTHERS COME AND DISPOSSESS YOU. The clause\'s syntax read as the cause ({SP_(60, 3, "ויבואו", "אחרים", "ויירשו", "אתכם")} "and others come and dispossess you"): the dispossession conditional — 12:29-30\'s warning read into 12:2 (81:3 says it again). Fresh.')
srow(60, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: MIGHT EVEN THE MOUNTAINS AND HILLS THEY WORSHIP BE DESTROYED? "THEIR GODS ON THE MOUNTAINS" — NOT THE MOUNTAINS THEIR GODS; THEIR GODS UNDER EVERY LEAFY TREE — NOT THE TREE THEIR GOD. WHY IS THE ASHERAH FORBIDDEN? BECAUSE THE HAND OF MAN TOUCHED IT; WHATEVER MAN\'S HAND TOUCHED IS FORBIDDEN. R. AKIVA: WHEREVER YOU FIND A HIGH MOUNTAIN, A LOFTY HILL AND A LEAFY TREE, KNOW THAT IDOLATRY IS THERE. THE MOUNTAINS NOT FORBIDDEN, THE PLANTED TREE FORBIDDEN — Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:5 whole ({SP_(60, 4, "תפיסת", "יד", "אדם")} "the grasp of a man\'s hand"; {SP_(60, 4, "אני", "אהיה", "אבין", "לפניך")} "I will explain before you"): the verse\'s prepositions read as location, not object — a PARAMETER of the destruction (what is attached to the ground is not destroyed); THE INK: "under every leafy tree" the Kings\' formula (ten seats, computed), 12:2 the Torah\'s one. Fresh; Avodah Zarah 45a-46a at 10b.')

srow(61, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL TEAR DOWN THEIR ALTARS" (12:3) — A STONE HEWN FROM THE FIRST FOR IDOLATRY. The head row of piska 61 ({SP_(61, 1, "אבן", "שחצבה", "מתחלה", "לעבודה", "זרה")} "a stone hewn from the first for idolatry"): the four objects of 12:3 read as four cases — made for idolatry against made and then worshipped (61:1-4). Fresh.')
srow(61, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND BREAK THEIR PILLARS" — HEWN AND THEN WORSHIPPED. ({SP_(61, 2, "שהיתה", "חצובה", "ועבדה")} "that was hewn and he worshipped it"). Fresh.')
srow(61, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THEIR ASHERIM YOU SHALL BURN" — AN ASHERAH PLANTED FROM THE FIRST FOR IDOLATRY. ({SP_(61, 3, "שנעשית", "מתחלה", "לעבודה", "זרה")} "made from the first for idolatry"). Fresh.')
srow(61, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE IMAGES OF THEIR GODS YOU SHALL CUT DOWN" — PLANTED AND THEN WORSHIPPED. ({SP_(61, 4, "שהיתה", "נטועה", "ועבדה")} "that was planted and he worshipped it"). Fresh.')
srow(61, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD — FROM HERE THEY SAID: THREE ASHERIM — A TREE PLANTED FROM THE FIRST FOR IDOLATRY IS FORBIDDEN ("YOU SHALL BURN"); IF IT SPROUTED, HE REMOVES THE NEW GROWTH ("THE IMAGES YOU SHALL CUT DOWN"); IF ONLY AN IDOL WAS SET UNDER IT AND REMOVED, IT IS PERMITTED ("YOU SHALL DESTROY THEIR NAME FROM THAT PLACE; YOU SHALL NOT DO SO TO THE LORD"). Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:7\'s three Asherim from three clauses ({SP_(61, 5, "שלש", "אשרות", "הם")} "three Asherim there are"; {SP_(61, 5, "נוטל", "מה", "שהחליף")} "he removes what it renewed"): the chapter\'s verbs made a decision table — burn / cut the growth / permitted; the translator marks the smaller type an interpolation (Finkelstein) — read and marked, the rows stand. Fresh; Avodah Zarah 48a at 10b.')
srow(61, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'THREE HOUSES — BUILT FROM THE FIRST FOR IDOLATRY, FORBIDDEN ("DESTROY ALL THE PLACES"); RENOVATED, HE REMOVES THE RENOVATION ("DESTROY THEIR NAME"); ONLY AN IDOL BROUGHT IN AND OUT, PERMITTED ("TEAR DOWN THEIR ALTARS, BREAK THEIR PILLARS") — TORE DOWN THE ALTAR, LEAVE IT; BROKE THE PILLAR, LEAVE IT. MIGHT ONE BE BOUND TO PURSUE THEM OUTSIDE THE LAND? "FROM THAT PLACE" — IN THE LAND YOU PURSUE THEM, NOT OUTSIDE IT. Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:7\'s three houses and THE BOUNDARY OF THE DUTY ({SP_(61, 6, "שלשה", "בתים", "הם")} "three houses there are"; {SP_(61, 6, "בארץ", "ישראל", "אתה", "מצוה", "לרדף", "אחריהם")} "in the Land of Israel you are commanded to pursue them"): "from that place" a PARAMETER of scope — the Land; THE INK: "from that place" 12:3 and 17:10 alone (computed). Fresh.')
srow(61, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER: WHENCE THAT ONE WHO CUTS DOWN AN ASHERAH MUST UPROOT IT? "YOU SHALL DESTROY THEIR NAME." R. AKIVA: WHY? "DESTROY, YOU SHALL DESTROY" IS ALREADY SAID; "DESTROY THEIR NAME" — TO CHANGE THEIR NAME. MIGHT ONE CHANGE IT FOR THE BETTER? "UTTERLY DETEST IT, UTTERLY ABHOR IT" (7:26). THE FIFTH VERB\'S DISPUTE — the root or the name ({SP_(61, 7, "לשנות", "את", "שמם")} "to change their name"; {SP_(61, 7, "או", "יכול", "לשבח")} "or might it be for praise"): the renaming for the worse — Tosefta Avodah Zarah 6:4\'s examples (the English); THE INK: "destroy their name" the fifth verb 7:5 lacks (computed), the design\'s find. Read before at chapter 7 (the ledger holds 61:7 on 7:26), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(61, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WHO TEARS OUT A STONE OF THE SANCTUARY, THE ALTAR OR THE COURTS TRANSGRESSES A PROHIBITION? "YOU SHALL TEAR DOWN THEIR ALTARS … YOU SHALL NOT DO SO TO THE LORD YOUR GOD." R. ISHMAEL: WHENCE THAT ONE WHO ERASES ONE LETTER OF THE NAME TRANSGRESSES? "YOU SHALL DESTROY THEIR NAME … YOU SHALL NOT DO SO." RABBAN GAMLIEL: WOULD ISRAEL TEAR DOWN THEIR OWN ALTARS? RATHER — DO NOT DO AS THEY DO, LEST YOUR EVIL DEEDS CAUSE YOUR FATHERS\' SANCTUARY TO BE DESTROYED. 12:4 READ THREE WAYS ({SP_(61, 8, "למוחק", "אות", "אחת", "מן", "השם")} "one who erases one letter of the Name"; {SP_(61, 8, "חס", "ושלום")} "Heaven forbid"): the prohibition on the Sanctuary\'s stones and the Name\'s letters (Tosefta Makkot 5:8-9 — the English), against the reading as a warning — a DISPUTE on 12:4\'s object; THE INK: 12:4\'s plural against 12:31\'s singular, the pair\'s two seats (computed). Fresh.')

srow(62, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BUT TO THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CHOOSE FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES" (12:5) — SEEK BY A PROPHET. MIGHT YOU WAIT UNTIL A PROPHET TELLS YOU? "HIS DWELLING YOU SHALL SEEK, AND YOU SHALL COME THERE" — SEEK AND FIND, AND AFTERWARD THE PROPHET WILL TELL YOU. SO WITH DAVID: "I WILL NOT GIVE SLEEP TO MY EYES UNTIL I FIND A PLACE FOR THE LORD" (PSALM 132:4-5); AND THAT HE ACTED ONLY BY A PROPHET — "GAD CAME TO DAVID: GO UP, RAISE AN ALTAR ON THE THRESHING FLOOR OF ARAUNAH" (2 SAMUEL 24:18), "SOLOMON BEGAN TO BUILD ON MOUNT MORIAH WHICH APPEARED TO DAVID" (2 CHRONICLES 3:1). THE SEEKING\'S PROCEDURE — the head row of piska 62 ({SP_(62, 1, "דרש", "על", "פי", "נביא")} "seek by the mouth of a prophet"; {SP_(62, 1, "דרש", "ומצא", "ואחר", "כך", "יאמר", "לך", "נביא")} "seek and find, and afterward a prophet will tell you"): "you shall seek" read as an order of steps — the search first, the prophet\'s word after; THE RUN: David at the threshing floor the citation (2 Samuel 24 the run\'s own seat); THE INK: "His dwelling" one seat in the Bible (computed). Fresh.')
srow(62, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE VERSE SAYS "IN ONE OF YOUR TRIBES" (12:14), ANOTHER "FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES" (12:5) — HOW ARE BOTH UPHELD? THEY KNEW THE CHOSEN HOUSE WOULD BE BUILT IN JUDAH\'S AND BENJAMIN\'S PORTION, SO THEY SET APART THE FAT OF JERICHO; WHO ATE IT ALL THOSE YEARS? THE SONS OF THE KENITE, MOSES\' FATHER-IN-LAW (JUDGES 1:16), AND WHEN THE HOUSE WAS BUILT THEY LEFT — R. SHIMON; R. JUDAH: THEY WENT TO JABEZ TO LEARN TORAH (1 CHRONICLES 2:55). THE TWO VERSES RECONCILED BY JERICHO\'S PASTURE ({SP_(62, 2, "כיצד", "נתקימו", "שני", "כתובים", "הללו")} "how are these two verses upheld"; {SP_(62, 2, "הפרישו", "דשנה", "של", "יריחו")} "they set apart the fat of Jericho"): I13 (checked — two verses reconciled); the Kenites\' portion — Sifrei Bamidbar 78\'s parallel (the English); Judges 1:16 the run. Fresh.')
srow(62, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "IN ONE OF YOUR TRIBES" — "FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES": THE MONEY FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES, THE CHOSEN HOUSE FROM ONE TRIBE. ANOTHER: "IN ONE OF YOUR TRIBES" — SHILOH; "FROM ALL YOUR TRIBES" — JERUSALEM. "DAVID BOUGHT THE THRESHING FLOOR FOR FIFTY SHEKELS OF SILVER" (2 SAMUEL 24:24) AND "DAVID GAVE ORNAN SIX HUNDRED SHEKELS OF GOLD" (1 CHRONICLES 21:25) — TWELVE TRIBES, FIFTY FROM EACH, SIX HUNDRED FOR ALL. THE TWO VERSES TWICE MORE ({SP_(62, 3, "הכסף", "מכל", "שבטיכם")} "the money from all your tribes"; {SP_(62, 3, "זו", "שילה")} "this is Shiloh"; {SP_(62, 3, "נטל", "חמשים", "שקלים", "מכל", "שבט", "ושבט")} "he took fifty shekels from each tribe"): I13 (checked) — the funding and the ground; Shiloh and Jerusalem (the two stations the chapter\'s 12:9 and 12:11 will be read as); the fifty and the six hundred reconciled by arithmetic — 12 × 50 = 600 (the answer sheet Sifrei Bamidbar 42 — the English). Fresh.')
srow(62, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO PUT HIS NAME THERE" — "HIS NAME" HERE AND "MY NAME" AT NUMBERS 6:27: AS HIS NAME HERE IS THE CHOSEN HOUSE, SO MY NAME THERE; AS MY NAME THERE IS THE PRIESTLY BLESSING, SO HIS NAME HERE. ONLY IN THE SANCTUARY? IN THE PROVINCES WHENCE? "IN EVERY PLACE WHERE I CAUSE MY NAME TO BE MENTIONED" (EXODUS 20:21). THEN WHY "TO PUT HIS NAME THERE"? IN THE SANCTUARY THEY SAY THE NAME AS WRITTEN, IN THE PROVINCE BY ITS SUBSTITUTE. THE NAME PRONOUNCED — I2 (checked — gezerah shavah on "name") ({SP_(62, 4, "נאמר", "כאן", "שמו", "ונאמר", "להלן", "שמי")} "it is said here His name and there My name"; {SP_(62, 4, "במקדש", "אומרים", "את", "השם", "ככתבו")} "in the Sanctuary they say the Name as written"): the priestly blessing\'s Name bound to the place — Mishnah Sotah 7:6 the answer sheet (the English); Exodus 20:21 the kin by CALL (the altar in every place — read through the Mekhilta, credited); Sifrei Bamidbar 43 read at Numbers 6 (the ledger names 12:5). Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(59, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(60, r) for r in range(1, 5)] + [(61, r) for r in range(1, 9)] + [(62, r) for r in range(1, 5)], sorted(S)
